our concrete, real gaps rather than rebuilding from scratch.\n\n**compliance-tracker** (PR [#605](https://github.com/FChecklist/compliance-tracker/pull/605)):\n- Upgraded the negative-variation warning into a real `409` hard block inside `createBoqRevision`'s transaction, with an explicit `allowScopeReductionOverride` escape hatch\n- Generalized `compareBoq` to diff any two revisions, not just adjacent ones\n- Added a computed `totalVariation` (running total variation value)\n- Added the missing `/api/v1/projexa/scope/[id]/{revisions,compare}` routes PROJEXA needs\n- 5 new pure unit tests, all passing; tsc clean; CI guardrail scripts pass\n\n**projexa** (PR [#57](https://github.com/FChecklist/projexa/pull/57)):\n- Proxy routes for the new endpoints\n- Extended the existing Scope of Work screen with a variation column, New Revision dialog, and Compare dialog, surfacing the 409 block with an override action\n- 6 new route tests + full existing suite passing, tsc clean\n\nBoth PRs are open, not merged — awaiting supervisor audit as instructed. PROGRESS.md in both repos documents the honest limitations (no separate Rev0/Rev1 label column; approval workflow not re-exposed).","ttft_ms":2931,"ttft_stream_ms":2213,"time_to_request_ms":29,"type":"result","duration_ms":1097443,"uuid":"f2e7c1fa-86dc-47ae-a4ef-58bfb498f205"}
